WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.129
Operational context management starts with reusable patterns.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:13.606
Prompt templates, context logs, source inventories, reusable context packs, and versioned summaries make large-context work more repeatable.

00:00:13.606 --> 00:00:22.542
A context pack might include current instructions, project assumptions, key source summaries, known constraints, and open questions.

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:26.130
Versioning matters because context changes over time.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.228
Human review remains necessary.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:36.148
Large context can produce impressive summaries, but reviewers should verify important claims against source material.

00:00:36.148 --> 00:00:43.121
Ask the model to ground claims in provided sources, cite sections when possible, and state uncertainty.

00:00:43.121 --> 00:00:53.207
For professional workflows, the review process should include what material was included, what was excluded, and which assumptions shaped the answer.

00:00:53.207 --> 00:00:56.456
Privacy and sensitive data handling are central.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:01:06.136
Context may be logged, retained, displayed, sent to a provider, stored in chat history, or reused by surrounding systems depending on the tool.

00:01:06.136 --> 00:01:16.561
Context minimization means including only what the task requires and avoiding unnecessary secrets, personal data, client information, or internal records.

00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:19.404
Large windows make it easier to overshare.

00:01:19.404 --> 00:01:23.534
Documenting assumptions and excluded material improves trust.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:28.678
If a summary is based on three policies but excludes two appendices, say so.

00:01:28.678 --> 00:01:32.740
If retrieved evidence came from a specific index, record it.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.245
If old context may be stale, mark it.

00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:43.300
Good context operations make the model's working set visible, so reviewers can understand the boundaries of the answer.
